-Fetching and Pulling from Your Remotes
As you just saw, to get data from your remote projects, you can run:

git fetch <remote>

remote is set to origin when you clone the repo

- git pull: Download the latest changes and automatically merge them into your current branch.

git pull origin main --rebase

--rebase → Replay your local commits on top of the updated main branch instead of merging.


Inspecting a Remote
If you want to see more information about a particular remote, you can use the git remote show <remote> command. If you run this command with a particular shortname, such as origin 
git remote show origin

- Renaming and Removing remotes

